-- =============================================
-- Spotify DBS — Seed data, part 2: accounts, auth, and activity
-- Run AFTER 05_seed_catalog.sql.
--
-- Demo accounts are real Supabase Auth users, not just public.users rows —
-- the design doc commits to "passwords are not stored in our schema at all"
-- (section 6), so seeding has to go through auth.users too, not just our own
-- tables. This is the standard trick for seeding Supabase Auth directly from
-- SQL: insert into auth.users with crypt()/gen_salt() (pgcrypto, enabled in
-- 01_schema.sql) instead of going through the signup API, and give each user a
-- matching auth.identities row for the 'email' provider so Studio and GoTrue
-- treat the account exactly like one created through supabase.auth.signUp().
--
-- Every seeded account's password is: demo-password-123
-- =============================================

-- ── Plan (BR: referenced by every subscription) ──

